Skip the intersection of an edge with a face it is proven clear of.

What it fixes
  BOPAlgo_PaveFiller::PerformEF intersects every edge with every face
  whose bounding boxes overlap. On a B-spline face that is
  IntCurveSurface_HInter: a polygon of the edge against a polyhedron of
  the face, and an exact root search (math_FunctionSetRoot) from every
  place the two come within their deflections of each other. An edge
  that runs beside the face without meeting it starts thousands of
  searches, each of which fails only after its iterations run out. One
  circle 0.12 mm from one face of a lofted skin, in a keycap whose
  recesses follow a second skin 0.6 mm inside the first, started 21,805
  searches and took 0.64 s to find nothing; of the 1,172 edge/face pairs
  in that part's last cut, 855 had no common part and took 5.2 s of the
  6.6 s the pairs cost on one thread.

  IntTools_Apart.hxx proves such a pair apart, exactly: each piece is
  enclosed in a box that is certain to hold it (the control points of a
  Bezier piece cut from the B-spline; the corners of a line, circle,
  ellipse, plane, cylinder, cone, sphere or torus piece, grown by the
  bound of its second derivative), and a pair of boxes that will not
  separate is halved until it does, or a budget of comparisons or a
  depth of halvings runs out. Nothing is sampled. BOPAlgo_EdgeFace::Perform asks for that proof first, at a
  gap of ten times the tolerances inside which IntTools_EdgeFace reports
  a common part and never less than 0.001, and returns "done, no common
  part" on a proof, which is what the intersection returns for such a
  pair. Anything not proven is intersected as before.

  The one other thing PerformEF keeps from an intersection with no
  common part is the least distance it happened to measure, which
  ProcessExistingPaveBlocks later compares with the tolerance of a
  section edge. A proven pair has no measurement, so it keeps half the
  proven gap, negated. Where the comparison is made, a gap above the tolerance
  answers it the way any measurement above the gap would; the
  intersection is run after all (MeasuredEdgeFace) only if the gap is
  within that tolerance, or if a later range of the same edge could
  answer differently depending on whether this one had measured
  anything. Neither happened on anything measured below.

How it was measured
  The keycap's last cut (14 tools, 136 faces, against 99 faces): 806 of
  the 1,172 pairs proven, in 39 ms in all and 0.1 ms at worst; the cut
  1.75 s before and 0.87 s after on fourteen threads, its union with
  the wheels 0.74 s and 0.32 s. Faces, edges, vertices, volume and area
  of every result equal to the last printed digit, with the proofs
  skipping, with every proof followed by its intersection
  (PARCAD_APART_VERIFY=1, which reports any proof the intersection
  disagrees with: none), and with every negated gap measured where it is
  read (PARCAD_APART_VERIFY=measure). parcad's corpus and its recorded
  replies are in vendor/occt-sys/PARCAD-CHANGES.md.

  What it does not fix: a pair that does meet, and runs close to the
  face on the way, still starts the same failing searches. Those are
  what is left of the edge/face time.

Upstream status
  Not yet reported.

